Negative control for product-template.test.ts.

Declares the pick with the left-hand two-column layout as its fallback, so a
brand with no template, an empty one, or a name the page does not lay out gets
that instead of the right-hand two-column layout. Every named template still
draws its own layout.

Intended RED (product-template.test.ts, "productTemplate"):
  draws the right-hand two-column layout for no template
  draws the right-hand two-column layout for an empty template
  draws the right-hand two-column layout for a template only other pages carry
  draws the right-hand two-column layout for a name no layout carries
  draws the right-hand two-column layout for a name every object inherits
Intended GREEN:
  draws the layout the <each> template carries

diff --git a/apps/cart/src/shell/modules/product/shell.ts b/apps/cart/src/shell/modules/product/shell.ts
